# ── Sensitive conversations ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Files matching *.private.md are excluded from git entirely. They still live in
# the vault, are fully searchable, and sync via Obsidian — they just never enter
# git history, which is the one place deletion doesn't actually delete.
#
# Why a wildcard and not a list of filenames: this file IS committed. Enumerating
# the sensitive notes here would publish their filenames, and the slugs describe
# their contents. The suffix carries the boundary instead.
#
# Why a filename suffix and not .git/info/exclude: info/exclude is never committed,
# so the protection would silently disappear on a fresh clone. Protection you can
# lose without noticing is worse than none.
Library/*.private.md

# ── Obsidian local state ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
.obsidian/workspace.json
.obsidian/workspace-mobile.json
.trash/
.DS_Store

# ── From remote auto-sync ──────────────────────────────────────────────
.obsidian/plugins/
*.icloud
